# WHAT: template for the gitignored .dev.vars — the LOCAL-DEVELOPMENT
# secret file. `.dev.vars` is a wrangler dev feature: wrangler loads it
# when `npm run dev` starts and never when deploying, so this file has no
# effect on production. Copy it to `.dev.vars` and paste a real value.
#
# The value is the base64 of 32 random bytes: the AES-256-GCM key the
# plane uses to seal REALITY private keys at rest (src/env.ts
# secretBytes() fails loudly when it is missing or malformed). Use a
# DIFFERENT value locally and in production — never your real
# production key here.
#
# Generate a value:
#   node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#
# Production is a separate file with a separate value: .env.production,
# passed to the FIRST deploy via
#   npx wrangler deploy --secrets-file .env.production
# and rotated afterwards with `npx wrangler secret put REALITY_KEY_SECRET`.
# .env.production is read only when you pass it explicitly — it is not
# loaded by dev, tests, or typecheck. Both files are gitignored.
#
# Warnings:
#  - Rotating a REALITY_KEY_SECRET in production strands every sealed key
#    ever stored (they are unreadable without it). Generate once per
#    deployment, keep it backed up, rotate only with a plan.
#  - Never pipe this value into wrangler from PowerShell 5.1: the pipe
#   prepends a UTF-8 BOM and the decoder rejects it. Use the interactive
#   prompt (`npx wrangler secret put`) or a dotenv file.
REALITY_KEY_SECRET=base64-of-32-random-bytes
